// Days 351–410
export default [
{t:"Where were you?",n:"God finally answers Job from the whirlwind, not with explanations but with questions: 'Where were you when I laid the foundations of the earth?' He shows Job the stars, the sea, the animals. God's greatness is the answer to our pain.",q:"How does seeing God's greatness change how you see your problems?",a:"Look at the night sky tonight and worship the God who made it.",p:"You laid the foundations of the earth. I trust You with my life."},
{t:"Hand over mouth",n:"Job answers God: 'Behold, I am vile; what shall I answer You? I lay my hand over my mouth.' Sometimes the right response to God is humble silence.",q:"Is there a question you need to stop demanding God answer?",a:"Spend five minutes in silence before God without asking anything.",p:"I lay my hand over my mouth. You are God."},
{t:"Sons, not slaves",n:"God describes Leviathan, a creature no one can tame, yet God rules it. Paul writes, 'God has sent forth the Spirit of His Son into your hearts, crying out, Abba, Father! Therefore you are no longer a slave but a son.' Psalm 116: 'I love the Lord, because He has heard my voice.'",q:"Do you relate to God as a slave trying to earn or as a child who is loved?",a:"Pray today using 'Abba, Father' and speak to Him as a loved child.",p:"Abba, Father, I am Your child, not a slave."},
{t:"Seeing God, praying for friends",n:"Job says, 'I have heard of You by the hearing of the ear, but now my eye sees You.' God restored Job when he prayed for his friends. Ecclesiastes begins: 'Vanity of vanities, all is vanity.'",q:"Have you moved from hearing about God to seeing Him for yourself?",a:"Pray for a friend who has hurt or misunderstood you.",p:"I've heard of You, but now let my eyes see You."},
{t:"Walk in the Spirit",n:"Solomon tried pleasure, building and wealth: 'All was vanity and grasping for the wind.' Paul: 'Walk in the Spirit, and you shall not fulfil the lust of the flesh... The fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, self-control.'",q:"Which fruit of the Spirit is growing most in you, and which least?",a:"Choose one fruit to practise deliberately today.",p:"Holy Spirit, I walk with You today. Grow Your fruit in me."},
{t:"A time for everything",n:"'To everything there is a season, a time for every purpose under heaven.' God 'has made everything beautiful in its time. Also He has put eternity in their hearts.' Psalm 117, the shortest psalm, calls all nations to praise God.",q:"What season are you in, and what is it for?",a:"Embrace your current season today instead of wishing it away.",p:"You make everything beautiful in its time."},
{t:"Sowing and reaping",n:"'Do not be rash with your mouth... God is in heaven, and you on earth; therefore let your words be few.' Paul writes, 'Whatever a man sows, that he will also reap... Let us not grow weary while doing good.'",q:"What are you sowing today that you'll reap later?",a:"Sow one good seed today: a kind word, a gift, or a prayer.",p:"I won't grow weary of doing good. Let me sow to the Spirit."},
{t:"Never satisfied without God",n:"Solomon saw people with wealth who could never enjoy it. 'All the labour of man is for his mouth, and yet the soul is not satisfied.' Only God satisfies.",q:"What are you chasing that never truly satisfies?",a:"Fast from one 'satisfaction-seeker' today and turn to God.",p:"Only You satisfy my soul."},
{t:"Every spiritual blessing",n:"Ephesians 1: 'Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has blessed us with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly places in Christ.' Paul prays that the eyes of your understanding would be opened. Psalm 118: 'This is the day the Lord has made.'",q:"Which spiritual blessing in Ephesians 1 means most to you today?",a:"List every blessing you find in Ephesians 1:3–14.",p:"This is the day You made. Thank You for every spiritual blessing."},
{t:"Enjoy life with God",n:"'Go, eat your bread with joy... Live joyfully... Whatever your hand finds to do, do it with your might.' Life under the sun is short; enjoy God's gifts while you have them.",q:"Are you enjoying the gifts God has given you?",a:"Enjoy a simple gift today with deliberate thanks.",p:"Help me live joyfully and work with all my might."},
{t:"Saved by grace, made for good works",n:"Ephesians 2: 'By grace you have been saved through faith, and that not of yourselves; it is the gift of God... For we are His workmanship, created in Christ Jesus for good works, which God prepared beforehand.' Jesus 'Himself is our peace'.",q:"What good works might God have prepared for you today?",a:"Look for and do one 'prepared' good work today.",p:"I am Your workmanship. Lead me into the works You prepared."},
{t:"Remember your Creator",n:"'Cast your bread upon the waters, for you will find it after many days.' 'Remember now your Creator in the days of your youth.' The conclusion: 'Fear God and keep His commandments, for this is man's all.'",q:"How are you investing your best years in God?",a:"Cast your 'bread' on the waters today through generosity.",p:"I remember You, my Creator, in all my days."},
{t:"Abundantly more",n:"The Song of Songs celebrates love. Paul prays you would know 'the love of Christ which passes knowledge' and be 'filled with all the fullness of God... to Him who is able to do exceedingly abundantly above all that we ask or think'. Psalm 119 celebrates God's Word in 176 verses.",q:"What 'exceedingly abundant' thing are you asking God for?",a:"Pray Ephesians 3:14–21 over your life today.",p:"You are able to do exceedingly abundantly more. I ask big."},
{t:"His banner over me is love",n:"'He brought me to the banqueting house, and his banner over me was love.' 'Rise up, my love, my fair one, and come away.' Jesus invites you into intimacy.",q:"Do you know yourself as Jesus' beloved?",a:"Spend time in worship simply receiving God's love.",p:"Your banner over me is love."},
{t:"Equipping the saints",n:"The beloved is searched for and found. Ephesians 4: Christ gave apostles, prophets, evangelists, pastors and teachers 'for the equipping of the saints for the work of ministry'. Speak the truth in love, and grow up into Christ.",q:"How are you being equipped for ministry, and how are you equipping others?",a:"Ask a church leader how you could serve or be trained.",p:"Equip me for the work of ministry, and help me speak the truth in love."},
{t:"I opened, but He was gone",n:"The bride hesitated to open the door, and when she did, her beloved had gone. Delay in responding to God's invitation has a cost. Psalm 120: 'In my distress I cried to the Lord, and He heard me.'",q:"Is Jesus knocking on a door you've been slow to open?",a:"Respond immediately to God's nudge today.",p:"I won't delay. I open the door to You now."},
{t:"Be filled with the Spirit",n:"Ephesians 5: 'Walk in love, as Christ also has loved us... Walk as children of light... Do not be drunk with wine... but be filled with the Spirit, speaking to one another in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs.'",q:"What fills you most during the day?",a:"Ask the Holy Spirit to fill you afresh before each part of your day.",p:"Fill me with Your Spirit. I want to overflow."},
{t:"Love as strong as death",n:"'Love is as strong as death... Many waters cannot quench love, nor can the floods drown it.' God's love for you is unquenchable.",q:"How does unquenchable love change how you see yourself?",a:"Show unquenchable love today to someone hard to love.",p:"Your love is stronger than death, and many waters cannot quench it."},
{t:"Though your sins are scarlet",n:"Isaiah begins with God's grief over His people's empty religion: 'Come now, and let us reason together... Though your sins are like scarlet, they shall be as white as snow.' Psalm 121: 'My help comes from the Lord, who made heaven and earth.'",q:"Is there any empty religion in your life that God wants to replace with real relationship?",a:"Bring one 'scarlet' sin to God and receive His cleansing.",p:"Wash me white as snow. My help comes from You."},
{t:"The armour of God",n:"Isaiah sees nations streaming to God's mountain to learn His ways. Ephesians 6: 'Be strong in the Lord and in the power of His might. Put on the whole armour of God... praying always with all prayer and supplication in the Spirit.'",q:"Which piece of armour do you most need to 'put on' today?",a:"Pray through each piece of armour (Ephesians 6:14–18) this morning.",p:"I put on Your whole armour and stand firm in Your might."},
{t:"Washed and sheltered",n:"Isaiah warns of judgment on proud Jerusalem, then promises: 'The Lord will create above every dwelling place of Mount Zion... a cloud and smoke by day and the shining of a flaming fire by night... a shelter.'",q:"Where do you need God's shelter today?",a:"Pray a covering of God's presence over your home.",p:"Cover my home with Your cloud by day and fire by night."},
{t:"To live is Christ",n:"Isaiah sings of God's vineyard that produced wild grapes. Paul writes from prison: 'He who has begun a good work in you will complete it... For to me, to live is Christ, and to die is gain.' Psalm 122: 'I was glad when they said to me, Let us go into the house of the Lord.'",q:"What would it mean for you that 'to live is Christ'?",a:"Ask God to show you what good work He's completing in you.",p:"For me to live is Christ. Complete Your good work in me."},
{t:"Here am I, send me",n:"Isaiah saw the Lord high and lifted up and cried, 'Woe is me!' A coal from the altar touched his lips. God asked, 'Whom shall I send?' Isaiah said, 'Here am I! Send me.' Then the promise: 'A virgin shall conceive.'",q:"Have you said 'Here am I, send me' to God?",a:"Pray Isaiah's prayer today and mean it.",p:"Here am I, Lord. Send me."},
{t:"The mind of Christ",n:"Isaiah says, 'Bind up the testimony.' Paul writes, 'Let this mind be in you which was also in Christ Jesus, who... made Himself of no reputation, taking the form of a bondservant... Therefore God also has highly exalted Him.'",q:"Where do you need to humble yourself like Jesus?",a:"Take the lowest place in one situation today.",p:"Give me the mind of Christ: humble, obedient and loving."},
{t:"Unto us a Son",n:"'For unto us a Child is born, unto us a Son is given; and the government will be upon His shoulder. And His name will be called Wonderful, Counsellor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace.' Psalm 123: 'Our eyes look to the Lord our God.'",q:"Which name of Jesus in Isaiah 9:6 do you need most today?",a:"Worship Jesus by each of His five names.",p:"Wonderful Counsellor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace."},
{t:"Knowing Him",n:"'There shall come forth a Rod from the stem of Jesse... The Spirit of the Lord shall rest upon Him.' Paul: 'I count all things loss for the excellence of the knowledge of Christ Jesus my Lord... that I may know Him and the power of His resurrection.'",q:"Is knowing Christ your highest goal?",a:"Count one thing as 'loss' today for the sake of knowing Christ.",p:"That I may know You and the power of Your resurrection."},
{t:"Wells of salvation",n:"Isaiah 12 is a short song: 'Behold, God is my salvation, I will trust and not be afraid... Therefore with joy you will draw water from the wells of salvation.'",q:"How can you draw joy from God's salvation today?",a:"Sing or say Isaiah 12 out loud as praise.",p:"With joy I draw water from the wells of salvation."},
{t:"The peace that guards",n:"Isaiah prophesies against Babylon. Paul writes, 'Rejoice in the Lord always... Be anxious for nothing, but in everything by prayer and supplication, with thanksgiving, let your requests be made known to God; and the peace of God... will guard your hearts.' Psalm 124: 'If it had not been the Lord who was on our side...'",q:"What anxiety needs to be turned into prayer with thanksgiving?",a:"Practise Philippians 4:6–7 with your top worry today.",p:"I bring my requests with thanks. Guard my heart with Your peace."},
{t:"The fall of Lucifer",n:"Isaiah 14 describes the fall of a proud king, often seen as a picture of Satan: 'How you are fallen from heaven, O Lucifer... You have said, I will ascend... I will be like the Most High.' Pride is the root of rebellion.",q:"Where does pride try to make you 'like God' in your own life?",a:"Choose humility in one specific situation today.",p:"Guard me from pride. You alone are the Most High."},
{t:"Christ the image of God",n:"Isaiah weeps for Moab. Paul writes that Christ 'is the image of the invisible God... All things were created through Him and for Him. And He is before all things, and in Him all things consist.' Paul prays we'd be filled with the knowledge of His will.",q:"How does Christ's supremacy over everything affect your worries?",a:"Read Colossians 1:15–20 and worship Jesus as Lord of all.",p:"In You all things hold together, including my life."},
{t:"Those who trust are like Mount Zion",n:"Isaiah warns that those who forget God plant pleasant gardens that wither. Psalm 125: 'Those who trust in the Lord are like Mount Zion, which cannot be moved, but abides forever.'",q:"Is your trust in God steady or shaky right now?",a:"Do one thing today that requires trusting God.",p:"Make me like Mount Zion, unshakeable in You."},
{t:"Complete in Him",n:"Isaiah prophesies that Egypt and Assyria will one day worship God alongside Israel. Paul writes, 'You are complete in Him... having disarmed principalities and powers, He made a public spectacle of them, triumphing over them in it.'",q:"Do you live as if you're complete in Christ, or always lacking?",a:"Declare Colossians 2:10 and 2:15 over your life today.",p:"I am complete in You. You triumphed over every power."},
{t:"Prophetic acts",n:"God told Isaiah to walk barefoot for three years as a sign. Prophets sometimes acted out God's message. Obedience can look strange to others.",q:"Has God asked you to do something that looks strange to others?",a:"Obey God today even if it's misunderstood.",p:"I'll obey You even when it looks foolish."},
{t:"Set your mind above",n:"Isaiah watches through the night like a watchman. Colossians 3: 'Set your mind on things above... Put on tender mercies, kindness, humility, meekness, longsuffering... Let the word of Christ dwell in you richly.' Psalm 126: 'Those who sow in tears shall reap in joy.'",q:"What are you 'sowing in tears' that God will turn into joy?",a:"Put on one virtue from Colossians 3:12 deliberately today.",p:"I set my mind on things above. Let me reap in joy."},
{t:"The key of David",n:"God gave Eliakim 'the key of the house of David... he shall open, and no one shall shut'. Jesus holds that key now (Revelation 3:7). He opens doors no one can shut.",q:"What door are you waiting for Jesus to open?",a:"Pray today for a specific open door for the gospel.",p:"You hold the key. Open the doors You want opened."},
{t:"Glory from the ends of the earth",n:"Isaiah sees the earth devastated by sin, yet hears songs from the ends of the earth: 'Glory to the righteous!' Even in judgment, God's people sing.",q:"Can you praise God even when the world seems to be falling apart?",a:"Sing praise today despite bad news.",p:"From the ends of the earth we sing Your glory."},
{t:"Seasoned with salt",n:"'He will swallow up death forever, and the Lord God will wipe away tears from all faces.' Paul writes, 'Continue earnestly in prayer... Let your speech always be with grace, seasoned with salt.' Psalm 127: 'Unless the Lord builds the house, they labour in vain.'",q:"Are you building your life with God or in your own strength?",a:"Let every word you speak today be gracious.",p:"Build my house, Lord, or I labour in vain."},
{t:"Perfect peace",n:"'You will keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on You, because he trusts in You.' 'Your dead shall live.' God is our everlasting strength.",q:"Where is your mind 'stayed' today?",a:"Refocus your mind on God every time it wanders today.",p:"Keep me in perfect peace as my mind stays on You."},
{t:"Turned from idols",n:"God lays 'a precious cornerstone' in Zion. Paul praises the Thessalonians who 'turned to God from idols to serve the living and true God', and whose faith was known everywhere.",q:"What idols have you turned from, and is any creeping back?",a:"Name and reject one modern idol in your life.",p:"I turn from idols to serve You, the living and true God."},
{t:"This is the way, walk in it",n:"'In returning and rest you shall be saved; in quietness and confidence shall be your strength.' 'Your ears shall hear a word behind you, saying, This is the way, walk in it.' Psalm 128: blessed is everyone who fears the Lord.",q:"What way is God whispering to you right now?",a:"Spend quiet time listening for 'This is the way.'",p:"In quietness and confidence is my strength."},
{t:"Gentle like a mother",n:"Isaiah warns against trusting Egypt's horses. Paul tells the Thessalonians, 'We were gentle among you, just as a nursing mother cherishes her own children... We were well pleased to impart to you not only the gospel of God, but also our own lives.'",q:"Are you sharing your life, not just your words, with those you disciple?",a:"Share a meal or time with someone you're helping grow in faith.",p:"Make me gentle and willing to share my life, not only my words."},
{t:"A king will reign in righteousness",n:"'A king will reign in righteousness... A man will be as a hiding place from the wind... the Spirit is poured upon us from on high, and the wilderness becomes a fruitful field.'",q:"Where do you need the Spirit poured out on your wilderness?",a:"Pray for the Spirit to be poured out on your church.",p:"Pour out Your Spirit and make my wilderness fruitful."},
{t:"Increase and abound in love",n:"Isaiah sees the King in His beauty. Paul prays, 'May the Lord make you increase and abound in love to one another and to all.' Psalm 129: they afflicted me, but they have not prevailed.",q:"Who do you need to love more abundantly?",a:"Pray 1 Thessalonians 3:12 over your relationships.",p:"Make me increase and abound in love to all."},
{t:"The desert will bloom",n:"'The desert shall rejoice and blossom as the rose... Strengthen the weak hands... Say to those who are fearful-hearted, Be strong, do not fear! Behold, your God will come.'",q:"Who needs you to say 'Be strong, do not fear' today?",a:"Encourage a fearful person with Isaiah 35:4.",p:"Make the desert bloom and use me to strengthen weak hands."},
{t:"Live to please God",n:"Assyria mocked God. Paul writes, 'This is the will of God, your sanctification... For the Lord Himself will descend from heaven with a shout... And thus we shall always be with the Lord. Therefore comfort one another with these words.'",q:"How does Christ's return give you hope and purpose today?",a:"Comfort someone who is grieving with the hope of 1 Thessalonians 4.",p:"You are coming back. I want to live to please You."},
{t:"Out of the depths",n:"Hezekiah spread Assyria's threats before God and prayed. God answered and healed him, adding fifteen years to his life. Psalm 130: 'Out of the depths I have cried to You... There is forgiveness with You.'",q:"What are you crying to God about 'out of the depths'?",a:"Pray for healing for someone who is sick today.",p:"Out of the depths I cry to You. Hear me and heal."},
{t:"Pray without ceasing",n:"Hezekiah foolishly showed his treasures to Babylon. Paul's final words: 'Rejoice always, pray without ceasing, in everything give thanks... Do not quench the Spirit. Do not despise prophecies. Test all things; hold fast what is good.'",q:"Which of these commands is hardest for you right now?",a:"Practise praying without ceasing: turn every activity into a prayer today.",p:"I rejoice, pray and give thanks. I won't quench Your Spirit."},
{t:"Comfort My people",n:"'Comfort, yes, comfort My people!... Those who wait on the Lord shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings like eagles, they shall run and not be weary, they shall walk and not faint.'",q:"Are you waiting on the Lord or running on empty?",a:"Wait on the Lord today in a set time of stillness.",p:"I wait on You. Renew my strength like the eagle."},
{t:"Fear not, I am with you",n:"'Fear not, for I am with you; be not dismayed, for I am your God. I will strengthen you.' 'Behold! My Servant... I have put My Spirit upon Him.' Paul says God is glorified in His people. Psalm 131: 'I have calmed and quieted my soul, like a weaned child with his mother.'",q:"What fear do you need to hand to God?",a:"Memorise Isaiah 41:10.",p:"I won't fear. You are with me, and You strengthen me."},
{t:"Called by name",n:"Break week. 'Fear not, for I have redeemed you; I have called you by your name; you are Mine. When you pass through the waters, I will be with you... Behold, I will do a new thing.'",q:"What 'new thing' is God doing in your life?",a:"Read Acts in one sitting this break week, starting today.",p:"You call me by name. I am Yours. Do a new thing."},
{t:"Hold fast to the truth",n:"God mocks idols made from half a log, the other half used for cooking. Paul warns of deception before Christ's return and urges believers to 'stand fast and hold the traditions which you were taught'.",q:"What half-truths have you been tempted to believe?",a:"Check one belief against Scripture today.",p:"Keep me standing fast in Your truth."},
{t:"Treasures of darkness",n:"'I will give you the treasures of darkness and hidden riches of secret places, that you may know that I, the Lord, who call you by your name, am the God of Israel.' Psalm 132 recalls David's vow to find a place for God.",q:"What treasure might God reveal to you in a dark season?",a:"Thank God for a lesson learned in a dark time.",p:"Give me treasures in darkness, and teach me in secret places."},
{t:"Pride before the fall",n:"Babylon, the proud 'lady of kingdoms', said in her heart, 'I am, and there is no one else besides me.' Judgment came suddenly. Pride blinds us to danger.",q:"Is there any area where you feel invulnerable?",a:"Humble yourself in prayer about an area where you feel strong.",p:"Guard me from pride, Lord."},
{t:"Don't grow weary",n:"'I am the Lord your God, who teaches you to profit, who leads you by the way you should go.' Paul writes, 'Do not grow weary in doing good,' and works hard so as not to be a burden.",q:"Where are you growing weary in doing good?",a:"Do one good thing today you'd rather skip.",p:"Lead me in the way I should go. Keep me from growing weary."},
{t:"Engraved on His palms",n:"'Can a woman forget her nursing child?... Surely they may forget, yet I will not forget you. See, I have inscribed you on the palms of My hands.' Psalm 133: 'How good and how pleasant it is for brethren to dwell together in unity!'",q:"How does it feel to know you are engraved on God's hands?",a:"Do something today to build unity among believers.",p:"You will never forget me. Make us one."},
{t:"Chief of sinners",n:"'Listen to Me... look to the rock from which you were hewn.' Paul writes, 'Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners, of whom I am chief. However, for this reason I obtained mercy, that in me first Jesus Christ might show all longsuffering.'",q:"How does God's mercy to you make you merciful to others?",a:"Share your testimony of mercy with someone.",p:"Thank You for saving me, the chief of sinners."},
{t:"By His stripes",n:"'How beautiful upon the mountains are the feet of him who brings good news.' Isaiah 53: 'He was wounded for our transgressions, He was bruised for our iniquities... and by His stripes we are healed.'",q:"Which phrase of Isaiah 53 moves you most?",a:"Read Isaiah 53 slowly and thank Jesus for each line.",p:"By Your stripes I am healed. Thank You, Jesus."},
{t:"Pray for all people",n:"'Enlarge the place of your tent... For your Maker is your husband.' Paul urges prayers 'for all men, for kings and all who are in authority... God desires all men to be saved'. Psalm 134: 'Lift up your hands in the sanctuary, and bless the Lord.'",q:"Do you pray for leaders and authorities regularly?",a:"Pray for your national and local leaders by name today.",p:"Enlarge my tent. I pray for all people and every leader."},
{t:"Come to the waters",n:"'Ho! Everyone who thirsts, come to the waters... Seek the Lord while He may be found... My thoughts are not your thoughts... My word shall not return to Me void.'",q:"Where do you need to trust God's higher thoughts?",a:"Speak God's Word over a situation, believing it won't return void.",p:"Your Word will not return void. Your thoughts are higher."},
{t:"Qualified to lead",n:"'My house shall be called a house of prayer for all nations.' 'I dwell in the high and holy place, with him who has a contrite and humble spirit.' Paul lists the character qualities needed in church leaders.",q:"Which leadership quality in 1 Timothy 3 do you most need to grow in?",a:"Pick one quality from 1 Timothy 3 and practise it today.",p:"Make me a person of character, fit to serve You."},
];
